│  • This method only retrieves messages by strictly slicing the     │
│    list of S3 keys (events) according to the limit and offset.     │
│                                                                    │
│  2 What is the relationship between this part of the code and the  │
│    bug?                                                            │
│                                                                    │
│  • The bug describes toolUse and toolResult being stored / treated │
│    as separate events.                                             │
│  • When retrieving the last 100 messages via list_messages (or     │
│    listEvents), the toolUse event can be cutoff if located beyond  │
│    the 100th event whereas toolResult remains in the list.         │
│  • Since list_messages slices keys strictly by their index without │
│    considering dependencies between paired messages, it can        │
│    separately retrieve toolResult events without their             │
│    corresponding toolUse events.                                   │
│  • This leads to invalid context passed to the Bedrock Model and   │
│    validation exceptions.                                          │
│  • So list_messages is the core code that produces the event       │
│    cutoff described in the bug.                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Given the issue description, what would be the intended         │
│    behavior of this part of the code?                              │
│                                                                    │
│  • The list_messages method should be enhanced to:                 │
│     • Check, after slicing the message keys by limit and offset,   │
│       if the first or last message in the batch is a toolResult    │
│       that depends on a toolUse event that was excluded due to the │
│       slicing.                                                     │
│     • If so, prepend or append the missing corresponding toolUse   │
│       event to the list or generate a dummy missing toolUse event  │
│       similar to generate_missing_tool_result_content.             │
│     • This ensures that the returned messages form a coherent      │
│       context without orphaned toolResult or toolUse events.       │
│  • The method preserves existing pagination and retrieval logic    │
│    but with extra logic to maintain paired event integrity.        │
